{"name":"Woodland Nymph","hex":"#69804b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a creature or object: growing, living, or existing in a woodland.","Having the character of a woodland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land covered with woody vegetation.","A low-density forest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodland"},{"term":"nymph","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any female nature spirit associated with water, forests, grottos, wind, etc.","A young girl, especially one who is attractive, beautiful or graceful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish using a nymph larva as bait."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nymph"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woodland","blocks":[{"text":"A woodland is, in the broad sense, land covered with woody plants, or in a narrow sense, synonymous with wood, a low-density forest forming open habitats with plenty of sunlight and limited shade. Some savannas may also be woodlands, such as savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg/330px-Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland"},{"title":"Nymph","blocks":[{"text":"A nymph is a minor female nature deity in ancient Greek folklore. Distinct from other Greek goddesses, nymphs are generally regarded as personifications of nature; they are typically tied to a specific place, landform, or tree, and are usually depicted as maidens. Because of their association with springs, they were often seen as having healing properties; other divine powers of the nymphs included divination and shapeshifting. In spite of their divine nature, they were not immortal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Three_nymphs%2C_marble_relief%2C_c._320%E2%80%93300_BC.jpg/330px-Three_nymphs%2C_marble_relief%2C_c._320%E2%80%93300_BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymph"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/500px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/1280px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/500px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Miombo woodland in Malawi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANyika_miombo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg/500px-Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg/1280px-Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg/500px-Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dry sclerophyll woodland in western Sydney.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Open_Woodland_in_Illinois_United_States.jpg/500px-Open_Woodland_in_Illinois_United_States.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.w